1. `For any vector array or any vector container in c++` : when you do `cout << s[i++] << '\n';` considering `i` is a iterator 
    of a loop then this will first print `s[i]` and then increment i by 1 becausae this is post increment. 
    
    
2. `Finding index of a character in a string` : `int i = s.find(s[i],i+1);` `s.find` will find index of character `s[i]` in 
    string s from `i+1 to s.size()-1` and store in `i` . But make sure you use this under certain constraints because find doesn't
    found s[i] this would create a issue be careful while using this could be used under two pointers . make sure i not declared 
    previously if using in loop then don't use `int` with `i`.
    
    
3. `Example 2 sum of all digits in a number` :  In recurssion always think that is it is possible to write original function in terms
    of its own term with little bit variation over the recurssion runs and hit base condition and give the intended answer . In below
    code we did `n/10 + n%10` because expecting that recursion of `n/10` will give sum of rest of digits and we extracted  `n%10`.
    
    	   int digit_sum(int n){
    if(n == 0) return 0;
    return digit_sum(n/10) + n%10 ; 
}


4. `Time complexity ` : `O(log(n))` as this will be called for number of digits in the number * 1 because time complexity of each function 
    is 1.
